      "side": 1,
      "message": "New logic for the power on/power cycle paths has been added. For these cases, we need to allow powering off a chassis that is not present or does not have input power.\n\nConsider the scenario where a chassis is unplugged/removed from a system. Present changes to false, but the power state of the removed chassis would still report `On`. Thus, we need to initiate a `Transition::Off` request to keep the power state updated, even for an absent chassis.\n\nAny chassis that are initially absent from the system are skipped during a power off/power cycle, since by default those chassis are already off.",
